1
00:00:01,126 --> 00:00:04,379
Clearly, you're quite
an observant young man.

2
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:05,923
You must look at things

3
00:00:05,965 --> 00:00:07,215
- very carefully.
- [Tartah gasps]

4
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:09,927
[TARTAH] That mysterious
flash of light...

5
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:13,180
I wonder how much
he really knows.

6
00:00:13,764 --> 00:00:16,475
[TARTAH] Say, Mr. Qifrey.

7
00:00:16,517 --> 00:00:18,727
You know, since you're here,

8
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:21,020
I have something to ask you.

9
00:00:25,776 --> 00:00:26,944
Do you?

10
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:29,738
Wonderful!

11
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:30,865
[TARTAH] Uh?

12
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:33,200
[QIFREY] Oh, I simply adore
talking about magic.

13
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:34,326
I would be more than happy

14
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:36,119
to answer any questions
you might have!

15
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:38,037
What would you like to know?

16
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:39,122
Go on! Tell me!

17
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:41,124
[Tartah stutters]

18
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:44,085
[TARTAH] I can't tell him,
it's not that kind of question.

19
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:46,213
Not with him sparklin'
away like that!

20
00:00:47,046 --> 00:00:50,467
Pardon.
You brought the young lady?

21
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:52,135
Please, come with me.

22
00:00:56,515 --> 00:00:58,517
[DOCTOR] What we have here
is a cold,

23
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:01,020
- brought on by exhaustion.
- [Coco breathes heavily]

24
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:02,521
[Qifrey sighs softly]

25
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:06,065
[DOCTOR] It's clear she hasn't
been getting enough sleep.

26
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:08,360
With rest
and some nutritious meals,

27
00:01:08,402 --> 00:01:10,445
her condition should improve.

28
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:13,574
I'd like to keep her here
overnight, just to be safe.

29
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:16,117
Thank you, doctor.

30
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:19,705
[DOCTOR] Honestly,
I don't know the first thing

31
00:01:19,747 --> 00:01:20,998
about what kind of training

32
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:22,583
you witches
put yourselves through,

33
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:24,919
- but she's a child.
- [door opens]

34
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:27,254
The adults in her life
would do well

35
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:29,339
not to lose sight of that fact.

36
00:01:29,965 --> 00:01:31,299
[door closes]

37
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:33,510
[Qifrey sighs deeply]

38
00:01:33,552 --> 00:01:35,512
- [TARTAH] Uh?
- Yes, quite so.

39
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:38,181
I'm sorry, Coco.

40
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:39,767
[scribbling]

41
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,022
[inhales, blows]

42
00:01:50,736 --> 00:01:52,738
[Tartah gasps softly]

43
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:56,533
[Coco breathes heavily]

44
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,622
Hopefully, that will at least
ease the fever a bit.

45
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,164
I don't understand.

46
00:02:03,206 --> 00:02:06,125
Why would she work herself
to the point of collapse?

47
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:08,629
[QIFREY] Our bodies
and minds are remarkable.

48
00:02:09,128 --> 00:02:12,215
But sometimes even their
very best isn't enough.

49
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:13,968
Until recently,

50
00:02:14,009 --> 00:02:17,304
Coco was entirely ignorant
to the reality of witches.

51
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:19,347
That cheerful demeanor
of hers...

52
00:02:19,890 --> 00:02:22,309
may hide great insecurity
and fear.

53
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:23,894
[Tartah gasps softly]

54
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:27,648
[TARTAH] I had no idea.

55
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:30,233
The Outsider
I keep hearing about.

56
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,777
Is it possible she...

57
00:02:31,819 --> 00:02:33,320
- [QIFREY] Tartah.
- [TARTAH] Uh?

58
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:36,323
[QIFREY] About that question
you wanted to ask me,

59
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:38,909
could we put it off a bit?

60
00:02:39,785 --> 00:02:41,411
This hardly seems the time.

61
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:44,623
[TARTAH] Right.

62
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:48,167
I agree with you.

63
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:50,087
- Some other day then.
- [bell tolling]

64
00:02:50,129 --> 00:02:51,338
[QIFREY] Uh?

65
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:55,216
[TARTAH] I'd better head home.

66
00:02:55,258 --> 00:02:57,302
Of course. Take care.

67
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:02,933
- [footsteps]
- [Tartah panting]

68
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:15,112
[TARTAH] For a moment,
I felt a coldness in his eyes

69
00:03:15,154 --> 00:03:17,031
that chilled me to the bone.

70
00:03:18,824 --> 00:03:21,160
Perhaps I was imagining things.

71
00:03:21,869 --> 00:03:23,662
[GATEKEEPER] Afraid not!

72
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:26,832
This ferry is exclusively
for witches.

73
00:03:26,874 --> 00:03:29,793
If you live on the island,
then where's your pointed cap?

74
00:03:29,835 --> 00:03:30,919
A PROMISE IN SILVER

75
00:03:31,128 --> 00:03:32,462
Won't be able to let you on
unless I see proof

76
00:03:32,504 --> 00:03:33,714
you're a witch.

77
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:34,923
It's right here.

78
00:03:36,008 --> 00:03:37,092
Uh...

79
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:40,345
- What? It's gone!
- [GATEKEEPER] Huh?

80
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:42,639
[TARTAH] I rode
this morning, I swear...

81
00:03:42,681 --> 00:03:45,308
Is that so? You really think
little brats like you

82
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:47,519
haven't tried that line
on me before?

83
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:51,481
[GATEKEEPER] Hey, get back here!

84
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:55,903
[TARTAH] I can't get home
without my hat.

85
00:03:55,944 --> 00:03:57,196
I have to find it!

86
00:03:57,988 --> 00:04:00,490
[DOCTOR] Her breathing
has settled nicely.

87
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,496
With continued rest,
she'll be well in no time.

88
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:09,041
Thank goodness.

89
00:04:09,083 --> 00:04:10,167
[DOCTOR] I must say.

90
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:13,128
The cool atmosphere
you've created in this room

91
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:14,379
doesn't hurt.

92
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:16,673
Witches certainly are amazing.

93
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,884
I'd say the same of you doctors.

94
00:04:18,926 --> 00:04:21,011
My abilities
can't make her better,

95
00:04:21,053 --> 00:04:22,096
but yours can.

96
00:04:22,221 --> 00:04:25,306
Come, now.
This will aid in her recovery.

97
00:04:25,348 --> 00:04:28,435
If only we could all make use
of such power.

98
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:34,357
- [QIFREY] Indeed.
- [running footsteps]

99
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:35,859
I need a doctor!

100
00:04:35,901 --> 00:04:38,612
The bar to the north is on fire!

101
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:42,741
We've been trying to help
the injured get out of there,

102
00:04:42,783 --> 00:04:44,159
but they're all drunk, so--

103
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:47,121
[man gasps]

104
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:50,373
Are you a witch?
And you use water magic!

105
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,583
That's perfect!

106
00:04:51,625 --> 00:04:54,253
Come with me and help us
put out the fire!

107
00:04:54,293 --> 00:04:56,255
Witches are supposed
to help people in trouble,

108
00:04:56,295 --> 00:04:58,257
- aren't they?
- Please, just wait a moment!

109
00:04:58,297 --> 00:04:59,591
I can't leave!

110
00:04:59,633 --> 00:05:01,593
I need to stay here
with my apprentice!

111
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:03,762
- [COCO] I'll be all right.
- [both gasp]

112
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:05,513
Go help those people.

113
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:08,183
That's what witches
are supposed to do.

114
00:05:10,309 --> 00:05:12,479
Very well. I'll do that.

115
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,439
And you get some rest.

116
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:16,108
[Coco sighs]

117
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:18,152
[QIFREY] Right.
Let's be on our way.

118
00:05:18,193 --> 00:05:19,527
[DOCTOR] Thank you, good sir!

119
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:20,988
[QIFREY]
How serious is the fire?

120
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:22,489
[MAN] It was still small
when I left,

121
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:23,907
but now, who knows?

122
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:26,827
- We need to hurry! Come on!
- [Coco breathes softly]

123
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:31,873
[COCO] I was trying to be brave,
but the truth is,

124
00:05:31,915 --> 00:05:34,918
I'm terrified to be alone
right now.

125
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:37,504
- [running footsteps]
- [panting]

126
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:41,133
[TARTAH] I've searched
everywhere I could think of,

127
00:05:41,175 --> 00:05:42,467
with no luck.

128
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:44,469
- This is the last place...
- [DOCTOR] Make haste!

129
00:05:47,681 --> 00:05:50,391
Excuse me, coming through.

130
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:06,074
Please let me find it.

131
00:06:06,533 --> 00:06:08,743
Oh. There you are!

132
00:06:10,369 --> 00:06:11,454
[Tartah sighs]

133
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:15,083
What a relief.
Now I can get back home.

134
00:06:19,129 --> 00:06:21,256
- [Coco groans softly]
- [TARTAH] Uh?

135
00:06:22,216 --> 00:06:24,301
[TARTAH]
That doesn't sound good.

136
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:29,514
Coco? How are you feeling?
[gasps softly]

137
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,434
[Coco groans softly]
Tartah?

138
00:06:33,476 --> 00:06:36,479
- Sorry.
- This is a nice surprise.

139
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:38,648
What are you... [coughs]

140
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:40,359
[TARTAH] You all right?

141
00:06:41,276 --> 00:06:44,112
That cold only seems
to be getting worse.

142
00:06:44,154 --> 00:06:46,740
Let's see. Where is everyone?

143
00:06:47,282 --> 00:06:49,159
What happened
to all the doctors?

144
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:51,119
And Mr. Qifrey?

145
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:53,621
[COCO] A fire broke out.

146
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:55,082
They all went to help.

147
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,124
[running footsteps]

148
00:06:56,291 --> 00:06:58,335
[TARTAH] That explains
all the commotion.

149
00:06:58,377 --> 00:07:00,879
Wonder how long they'll take
to get back.

150
00:07:00,921 --> 00:07:03,215
Perhaps I'd better
go fetch someone.

151
00:07:03,257 --> 00:07:05,926
- [Coco coughing]
- [TARTAH] Uh?

152
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:09,221
There must be a way to help.

153
00:07:09,263 --> 00:07:12,431
Oh! I know how we can bring
the fever down!

154
00:07:12,473 --> 00:07:14,226
Remember Tranquileaf?

155
00:07:14,268 --> 00:07:15,936
I used it on your leg.

156
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:18,688
But it can also help
with fever and coughing.

157
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:22,025
It must be around here
somewhere.

158
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,277
Ah!

159
00:07:28,031 --> 00:07:29,532
[Tartah gasps softly]

160
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:34,704
[TARTAH] There are no labels.

161
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,581
What is this?

162
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:39,458
What kind of hospital leaves
their medicines unlabeled?

163
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,420
What if they got mixed up?

164
00:07:42,921 --> 00:07:45,132
Some of them do seem
darker than others.

165
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:49,428
Can other people tell which ones
are which by their color?

166
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:52,764
[Tartah sighs]

167
00:07:53,098 --> 00:07:54,599
The same old story.

168
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:57,560
People look at the world
around them,

169
00:07:57,602 --> 00:08:00,397
never thinking
others might see it differently.

170
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:03,108
[WITCH 1] Silverwash, eh?

171
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:04,818
[WITCH 2] That leaves out
complex spells

172
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:06,611
with magic dyes, for a start.

173
00:08:06,653 --> 00:08:08,487
[WITCH 1] And it's hard
to see him getting very far

174
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:09,656
as a magic stationer.

175
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:10,991
[FEMALE WITCH]
It's not so bad now,

176
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:12,326
but when he gets older...

177
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:14,661
[WITCH 3] At least he's good
at carving pens.

178
00:08:16,537 --> 00:08:17,747
[WITCH 1] The fact is,

179
00:08:17,789 --> 00:08:20,041
there are certain things
that certain people

180
00:08:20,083 --> 00:08:21,335
just can't do.

181
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:24,338
You should concentrate
on the things that you can.

182
00:08:24,379 --> 00:08:26,214
Damn it all.

183
00:08:26,589 --> 00:08:30,260
The components in magic dyes
are often used in medicine.

184
00:08:30,302 --> 00:08:31,636
If I knew what they were,

185
00:08:31,678 --> 00:08:33,888
I'd have an idea
what they can do.

186
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:36,057
But as it stands, I'm helpless!

187
00:08:36,724 --> 00:08:38,310
In this world,

188
00:08:38,352 --> 00:08:40,395
where everything's
colored silver...

189
00:08:40,979 --> 00:08:43,522
there's not a single path
in sight.

190
00:08:46,485 --> 00:08:49,696
- [Tartah gasps softly]
- [weakly] Tartah...

191
00:08:52,449 --> 00:08:57,454
I'm sorry. You're suffering,
and here I am, pitying myself.

192
00:08:57,496 --> 00:08:59,956
[Coco coughing]

193
00:09:00,290 --> 00:09:01,582
[TARTAH] Uh?

194
00:09:02,042 --> 00:09:03,460
You must be thirsty.

195
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:07,422
I'll pour you some water.

196
00:09:07,464 --> 00:09:09,590
Here. Drink up.

197
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,301
[Coco exhales]

198
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:14,595
Thank you, Tartah.

199
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:18,099
[Tartah gasps softly]

200
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:20,435
[TARTAH] A Vapor Bubble.

201
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,020
Come to think of it,

202
00:09:22,229 --> 00:09:23,897
I see Granda using
one of these all the time

203
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:25,482
when he's making ink.

204
00:09:26,066 --> 00:09:29,861
Of course! I could simply
reverse the process!

205
00:09:30,529 --> 00:09:33,281
If I extract the water
from the medicine,

206
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:36,826
perhaps I can identify
its components!

207
00:09:38,203 --> 00:09:40,579
Tranquileaf's used
in powder form.

208
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:42,499
They dry it out and crush it.

209
00:09:42,541 --> 00:09:44,876
So a powder's
what I'm looking for!

210
00:09:46,503 --> 00:09:48,796
It's not these crystals.

211
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:52,633
It's not this stuff that shines
in the moonlight.

212
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:58,139
This one's still liquid,
so that can't be it.

213
00:09:58,181 --> 00:10:00,767
And Tranquileaf
has no particular odor,

214
00:10:00,808 --> 00:10:03,770
so I can rule out
the ones that smell pungent.

215
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,648
After all that.

216
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,865
There's still three left.

217
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:18,452
Damn. Damn!

218
00:10:18,493 --> 00:10:20,745
I've come so far,

219
00:10:20,787 --> 00:10:23,164
and now I'm stuck!

220
00:10:23,664 --> 00:10:24,916
I'm...

221
00:10:25,542 --> 00:10:26,793
done.

222
00:10:27,294 --> 00:10:28,462
♪

223
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:29,837
[water sloshes softly]

224
00:10:30,629 --> 00:10:32,466
[TARTAH] Forgive me, Coco.

225
00:10:33,925 --> 00:10:35,594
I gave it my best,

226
00:10:36,303 --> 00:10:38,430
but this is simply beyond me.

227
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:42,934
I don't know why I ever
let myself think otherwise.

228
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:45,520
I knew I couldn't do it.

229
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:48,440
I knew it right from the start.

230
00:10:52,444 --> 00:10:54,279
[COCO] But you were wrong.

231
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:56,406
There is a way...

232
00:10:56,948 --> 00:10:59,200
to turn the things
you can't do...

233
00:11:00,535 --> 00:11:03,121
into things you can. Magic.

234
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:04,498
[Tartah gasps softly]

235
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:06,707
[COCO] You have ink and a pen?

236
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:08,335
I do have some ink!

237
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:10,211
And a pen
that I've been carving.

238
00:11:15,342 --> 00:11:16,843
[Coco exhales softly]

239
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:20,721
[scribbling]

240
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,227
[Coco shivers]

241
00:11:26,269 --> 00:11:27,562
[TARTAH] Uh?

242
00:11:31,483 --> 00:11:32,942
Are you all right?

243
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:35,153
[COCO] Mm-hm.

244
00:11:36,446 --> 00:11:38,657
[TARTAH] What kind of spell
are you drawing?

245
00:11:38,697 --> 00:11:42,118
Whatever it is,
will it make you feel better?

246
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:44,204
[COCO] Mm-mm.

247
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:47,748
It's not for me.
Not just for me, anyway.

248
00:11:48,458 --> 00:11:50,585
The spell I'm drawing...

249
00:11:50,627 --> 00:11:53,463
is one that's going
to help the both of us.

250
00:11:55,173 --> 00:11:57,592
[Tartah gasps] Really?

251
00:11:59,511 --> 00:12:01,846
A spell that could help me
as well?

252
00:12:02,472 --> 00:12:04,265
What kind of magic is that?

253
00:12:04,307 --> 00:12:07,394
[Coco chuckles softly]
This is the Sigil of Earth.

254
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:09,728
It's incredible.

255
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:11,606
It can dig tunnels.

256
00:12:11,648 --> 00:12:15,318
Turn rocks into grains of sand.

257
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,445
And how is it gonna help us now?

258
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:20,490
Changing signs
changes the spell.

259
00:12:21,366 --> 00:12:25,245
I inverted the Signs of Crushing
from their usual position.

260
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:29,332
Normally, this spell turns
solid things to powder.

261
00:12:29,374 --> 00:12:32,293
So then
if you inverted the signs,

262
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:35,380
it would become a spell to turn
powdered things back

263
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:36,464
into their solid form!

264
00:12:36,506 --> 00:12:38,091
[COCO] Right.

265
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:40,510
And that's where you come in.

266
00:12:42,262 --> 00:12:45,390
You know what these components
originally looked like.

267
00:12:45,432 --> 00:12:48,059
This spell is for you, Tartah.

268
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:51,812
It's what will lead you
to the answer.

269
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:55,900
[COCO] Huh?

270
00:12:55,942 --> 00:12:57,068
[TARTAH] Hm?

271
00:12:57,694 --> 00:12:59,738
[COCO] That was
as big a mess as I am.

272
00:12:59,778 --> 00:13:02,282
All wobbly and uneven.

273
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:03,824
[TARTAH] In other words,

274
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:06,827
you need these same shapes
drawn more neatly?

275
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:10,582
[COCO] And ideally,
more symmetrical.

276
00:13:11,499 --> 00:13:13,167
[TARTAH] I don't really draw,

277
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:15,878
but I can see
the balance in things.

278
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:18,089
It's what I do all the time.

279
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:27,181
[Coco gasps softly]

280
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:31,978
Say, about this sign here...

281
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:34,314
Right now, it's just
at the top and bottom,

282
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:36,733
would it be all right to
add it on the sides, too?

283
00:13:36,775 --> 00:13:39,319
A three-dimensional object
needs to be shaped

284
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,154
from every possible angle.

285
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:42,989
In its current form,

286
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:46,284
the spell is likely failing
due to insufficient information.

287
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:47,994
But if we... [gasps]

288
00:13:48,035 --> 00:13:51,372
Sorry! I shouldn't be
adjusting your spell.

289
00:13:51,414 --> 00:13:53,124
Please, it's fine.

290
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,084
It's just a basic spell.

291
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:59,380
Besides, if you change a spell
to help it work,

292
00:13:59,422 --> 00:14:02,925
I'd say that makes it
your spell.

293
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:04,260
[Tartah gasps softly]

294
00:14:06,346 --> 00:14:07,888
Now give it a try.

295
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:10,891
Hm. I will.

296
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:19,526
♪

297
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,862
[scribbling]

298
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:06,947
[Tartah breathes shakily]

299
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:13,830
Coco...

300
00:15:16,207 --> 00:15:17,542
I did it.

301
00:15:17,584 --> 00:15:19,460
It only lasted for a second.

302
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:21,295
But I did it!

303
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:23,005
Well done! [coughs]

304
00:15:23,047 --> 00:15:25,299
[TARTAH] Oh, sorry!
The medicine.

305
00:15:25,884 --> 00:15:27,260
No Tranquileaf.

306
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:30,555
Good thing we checked,
or this could've ended badly.

307
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:33,516
I was so certain it had
to be one of them.

308
00:15:33,558 --> 00:15:34,893
Right!

309
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:38,979
The next step
is to use this spell

310
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:40,523
to search the storage room.

311
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:42,983
Now I know I can find
what we need!

312
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,943
[door opens, closes]

313
00:15:55,538 --> 00:15:57,707
[TARTAH]
This reminds me of home.

314
00:16:03,797 --> 00:16:04,881
Thornbark.

315
00:16:04,923 --> 00:16:06,382
Milliflower.

316
00:16:06,424 --> 00:16:07,926
Seabriar.

317
00:16:07,966 --> 00:16:09,176
Sleeping Willow.

318
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:10,804
Drizzlebee Hive.

319
00:16:11,805 --> 00:16:14,432
I've seen them all,
as drawings in books.

320
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:18,185
And now here they are,
right in front of me!

321
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,479
Amazing!

322
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:23,190
When I hold up this seal,

323
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:26,820
it's as though the world
finally comes into focus.

324
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:29,071
Everything I've learned...

325
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:32,074
is helping point me
toward the answer.

326
00:16:32,867 --> 00:16:35,495
Learning
how to do new things...

327
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:37,538
It feels...

328
00:16:38,623 --> 00:16:40,458
So incredible.

329
00:16:42,293 --> 00:16:43,878
I found you.

330
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,424
This is Tranquileaf, all right.

331
00:16:48,466 --> 00:16:50,092
Now, the only thing left to do--

332
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:52,512
[DOCTOR] Young man!
What do you think

333
00:16:52,553 --> 00:16:54,138
you're doing in there?

334
00:16:54,472 --> 00:16:56,014
[TARTAH] Uh...

335
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:58,601
[DOCTOR]
You thought everyone was gone?

336
00:16:58,643 --> 00:17:00,728
What a ridiculous idea.

337
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:03,564
We would never leave
the hospital entirely abandoned.

338
00:17:03,606 --> 00:17:06,150
And there is a reason
those bottles aren't labeled.

339
00:17:06,192 --> 00:17:08,486
It's so people don't fiddle
with them.

340
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:11,739
You could have caused a problem
far more dangerous

341
00:17:11,781 --> 00:17:13,741
than the one
you were trying to solve.

342
00:17:13,783 --> 00:17:16,786
[TARTAH] I'm sorry.
I suppose I panicked.

343
00:17:16,828 --> 00:17:18,872
[doctor sighs]
It's a good impulse

344
00:17:18,913 --> 00:17:20,790
to want to take care
of your friend.

345
00:17:20,832 --> 00:17:23,292
But medicines
can also be poison.

346
00:17:23,334 --> 00:17:25,336
It takes knowledge
and experience

347
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:27,129
to use them correctly.

348
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,631
That said, in this case,

349
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:31,133
Tranquileaf is exactly
what was called for.

350
00:17:31,759 --> 00:17:34,136
Do you know very much
about medicine?

351
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:35,930
Interested in becoming a doctor?

352
00:17:35,972 --> 00:17:38,474
[TARTAH]
Oh. Well, actually...

353
00:17:38,516 --> 00:17:40,727
Oh, I see, that hat.

354
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:44,605
I didn't realize I was
addressing an apprentice witch.

355
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:49,193
[Tartah breathes softly]

356
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,739
[DOCTOR] We managed
to get all the injured out.

357
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:55,199
[WITCH 1] Well done, everyone.

358
00:17:55,241 --> 00:17:57,577
[QIFREY]
Thank you for your support.

359
00:17:58,036 --> 00:18:00,162
Seems the fire is mostly out.

360
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:02,623
Mind if I leave things
in your hands from here?

361
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:04,500
My apprentice is rather--

362
00:18:04,542 --> 00:18:07,127
Where do you think you're going?
We're not done here!

363
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:10,088
There's still a huge mess
at the site to clean up!

364
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,675
This sort of thing's easy
for you witch types, right?

365
00:18:12,717 --> 00:18:14,928
Just wiggle your fingers
and problem solved!

366
00:18:14,969 --> 00:18:16,763
You have to lead the way
at times like these,

367
00:18:16,804 --> 00:18:19,766
use your powers for good!
We're all counting on you, son!

368
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:23,644
Ah, sir? I'm afraid that's
a bit of an oversimplification.

369
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:26,606
Outsiders don't understand
these things.

370
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:27,648
[Qifrey sighs]

371
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:29,734
You may go on
and take your leave.

372
00:18:29,776 --> 00:18:31,527
This is under control.

373
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:32,904
[QIFREY] My thanks again.

374
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:40,954
[QIFREY]
Things are easy for witches.

375
00:18:40,995 --> 00:18:42,538
Hardly.

376
00:18:43,873 --> 00:18:45,416
If they were,

377
00:18:45,458 --> 00:18:48,544
we wouldn't have
to worry or suffer as we do.

378
00:18:53,007 --> 00:18:54,884
[Qifrey exhales softly]

379
00:19:07,145 --> 00:19:09,147
[bird squawking]

380
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:12,359
[grunts]
I can breathe so easily!

381
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:13,694
Good to hear.

382
00:19:14,152 --> 00:19:16,238
Apparently, the medicine worked.

383
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:18,616
Thanks for your help, Tartah!

384
00:19:18,783 --> 00:19:19,909
[TARTAH] Well...

385
00:19:20,618 --> 00:19:24,038
Honestly, I'd say
you're the one who helped me.

386
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:25,581
[Coco sighs softly]

387
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:29,043
[Tartah chuckles]

388
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:31,337
Witches really are amazing.

389
00:19:32,463 --> 00:19:34,007
[Coco chuckles]

390
00:19:34,048 --> 00:19:36,009
You know, I couldn't agree more.

391
00:19:36,050 --> 00:19:37,885
[bell tolling]

392
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:41,764
[NOLNOA] Staying out all night.

393
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:43,683
You worried me half to death.

394
00:19:44,058 --> 00:19:45,476
[TARTAH] Sorry, Granda.

395
00:19:45,518 --> 00:19:48,688
I do appreciate you
keeping me apprised, Qifrey.

396
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:51,649
Of course. You'd do the same
if the roles were reversed.

397
00:19:51,691 --> 00:19:54,234
[TARTAH] Oh, that's right.
My question.

398
00:19:54,276 --> 00:19:56,821
I wanted to ask about
that unusual flash of light

399
00:19:56,863 --> 00:19:58,531
that appeared the other day.

400
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:00,407
[BOTH] Flash of light?

401
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:02,035
[TARTAH] Hm?

402
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:04,162
Actually, never mind.

403
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:07,373
You push yourself
entirely too hard, you know.

404
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:09,167
Don't endanger your health now.

405
00:20:09,207 --> 00:20:10,501
Thank you, my friend.

406
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:13,211
[TARTAH] I suppose
it's possible I imagined it.

407
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:15,589
Well, whether I did or I didn't,

408
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:17,675
I'll have to look into it
on my own.

409
00:20:17,717 --> 00:20:18,926
[NOLNOA] Tartah.

410
00:20:18,968 --> 00:20:20,427
The ferry's leaving.

411
00:20:20,469 --> 00:20:21,554
[TARTAH] Uh...

412
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:25,474
[COCO] Master! I'm sorry
to have kept you waiting.

413
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,518
[FERRYMAN] Boat's heading out.

414
00:20:33,983 --> 00:20:36,194
- [COCO] Tartah!
- [TARTAH] Huh?

415
00:20:36,234 --> 00:20:38,029
[COCO] See you soon!

416
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:46,746
[QIFREY] Right then.
Let's head home.

417
00:20:46,787 --> 00:20:47,997
[COCO] Let's!

418
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,382
- [TARTAH] Coco!
- [COCO] Huh?

419
00:20:58,424 --> 00:21:02,011
[TARTAH] Listen, I'm going
to carve a pen for you!

420
00:21:02,053 --> 00:21:05,848
And then, I'll cross this river
using my own magic.

421
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:09,476
And deliver it to you
personally! I promise!

422
00:21:10,103 --> 00:21:14,232
[Coco exclaims, chuckles]

423
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:19,653
I can't wait to see
what it looks like!

424
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:21,363
[Tartah chuckles]

425
00:21:23,116 --> 00:21:26,077
[NOLNOA] Well, now, you two have
grown rather close,

426
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:27,411
- have you?
- [TARTAH] Hm.

427
00:21:27,453 --> 00:21:29,371
She's amazing.

428
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:31,874
Still, though.

429
00:21:31,916 --> 00:21:34,418
Not as amazing
as she's going to become.

430
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:36,754
Huh?

431
00:21:37,463 --> 00:21:38,881
My dear boy.

432
00:21:38,923 --> 00:21:41,550
I suspect you'll be
amazing, too.

433
00:21:41,592 --> 00:21:43,052
[Tartah gasps softly]

434
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:44,595
[Tartah chuckles]

435
00:21:44,637 --> 00:21:46,013
♪

436
00:21:47,765 --> 00:21:49,100
[QIFREY] Poor girl.

437
00:21:49,142 --> 00:21:51,894
You've been tormented
by nightmares all this time?

438
00:21:51,936 --> 00:21:54,647
Dreams are difficult
to deal with.

439
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:57,150
Sleeping spells
are forbidden, after all.

440
00:21:57,942 --> 00:22:00,694
Still, I'm sure we can find
some way to help.

441
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:03,739
Necessity is the mother
of invention, as they say.

442
00:22:04,115 --> 00:22:06,742
[COCO] That's very kind.
But you know,

443
00:22:06,784 --> 00:22:09,078
I think I'll be all right now.

444
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,830
[QIFREY] Are you sure?

445
00:22:11,289 --> 00:22:13,331
[COCO] Yes, I am.

446
00:22:14,125 --> 00:22:17,211
Because I discovered
a ray of hope.

447
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:21,132
Inverting the signs
when you draw them

448
00:22:21,174 --> 00:22:23,092
reverses their effect.

449
00:22:23,134 --> 00:22:26,470
Surely, forbidden spells
work the same way!

450
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:32,852
If I draw inverse signs
of the seal in that book,

451
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:36,689
maybe I can reverse the spell
that turned my mom to stone!

452
00:22:36,981 --> 00:22:38,858
[TETIA] Coco!

453
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:41,359
Hej med dig!

454
00:22:42,945 --> 00:22:44,864
I've been so worried!

455
00:22:45,405 --> 00:22:46,866
Is your fever all gone?

456
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:48,159
- [COCO] Yes.
- Hurrah!

457
00:22:48,201 --> 00:22:51,162
Thank goodness! I'm so glad!

458
00:22:51,204 --> 00:22:53,247
[Agott sighs]

459
00:22:57,043 --> 00:23:00,129
[SASARAN] Your gift
didn't work out terribly well,

460
00:23:00,171 --> 00:23:01,505
now did it?

461
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:05,634
The days of peace
have not yet made fools

462
00:23:05,676 --> 00:23:07,887
of all the Pointed Caps.

463
00:23:08,346 --> 00:23:10,430
We can't sit idle.

464
00:23:10,472 --> 00:23:13,809
It seems further action
is called for.

465
00:23:13,851 --> 00:23:16,896
[IGUIN] I see. So then, you...

466
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:19,565
the embodiment
of forbidden magic...

467
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:22,068
will take that action?

468
00:23:22,109 --> 00:23:24,486
[SASARAN]
That's my intention.

469
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:25,988
During a test,

470
00:23:26,030 --> 00:23:29,700
an apprentice must leave
their master's protection.

471
00:23:30,243 --> 00:23:33,495
That is when we must strike.

472
00:23:35,373 --> 00:23:39,919
EPISODE 11:
THE TEST IN SERPENTBACK CAVE

